# Tool names that must NEVER be marked `lazy = true`.
#
# A lazy tool only installs when its shim is first invoked, so anything your
# shell, editor, or window manager runs during startup has to be installed up
# front — otherwise the first prompt blocks on a download (or the command
# quietly goes missing). The `10-core.toml` file is generated eagerly; these
# names are additionally excluded from `50-lazy.toml` so a `*-full` list can
# never make a startup dependency lazy.
fd
fzf
tmux
zoxide
direnv
ripgrep
